  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Shelter reconstruction programme in Sindh, Pakistan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Islamic Relief (IR) plans to address the long term shelter needs of the flood affected population in lower Sindh by providing permanent shelters to 220 vulnerable families, focusing on female-headed households using a conflict sensitive approach.  IR will model its shelters on a locally-appropriate design with disaster resilient features, which has been endorsed by the communities that also agreed on the selection criteria. The project will be implemented between June 2011 and February 2012.</narrative>
  </description>
